messages:
tara: opened PR to reconcile function-calling examples across JS/Python/Go. fixes for links + a small schema tweak. PTAL: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/901
morgan: quick note: I changed the output envelope to include `status` and made `payload` nullable to match some tool callers that return just metadata. snippet: ```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": { "type": "string" },
    "payload": { "type": ["object", "null"] },
    "trace_id": { "type": "string" }
  },
  "required": ["status"]
}
```
ben: Heads-up CI failed on the TS snippet: import path `import { call } from 'redwood-sdk'` is outdated. New package is `@redwood/inference`. Error: `Module not found: Can't resolve 'redwood-sdk'`
anika: wording nit: in guardrails section we currently say "enforce schema strictly" which is triggering support queries. Suggest: "validate responses and fall back to a minimal envelope when parsing fails" + show fallback example.
tara: Good catch. Also let's include a small migration blurb under "v2 structured output" that shows a JS safe-check and a Python fallback helper.
morgan: added examples in the PR body. JS inline example: ```js
const resp = await invokeTool(...);
if (!resp.payload) {
  // fallback minimal envelope
  return { status: 'empty', payload: null };
}
return resp;
```
Python parse helper example: ```py
from redwood import parse_or_minimal
obj = parse_or_minimal(response_json, schema)
# obj['payload'] may be None
```
ben: reworked the TS examples to use `@redwood/inference` and updated the compile target. local doc-tests pass now.
docs-bot: Reminder: docs build queued on merge; staging deploy will run after CI.
ci-bot: PR #901 checks: docs-tests failed -> now passing after fixes.
anika: can we soften language in the guardrails intro — remove the word "reject" and add a short paragraph about observable regressions & suggested alerts.
morgan: done. Also fixed two broken anchors in /guides/tool-related (they were renamed). Left a TODO comment in the PR to add unit tests for JS parse examples.
tara: I'll review and merge this afternoon. If merged before 17:30 UTC it goes to the next deploy window. Thanks all for quick turn. :rocket:
morgan: follow-up: opening a micro-PR to add the unit tests mentioned in the TODO.
